{{!-- Leed's recommendation cards, from /leed:create recommendations (site-patterns rule 3). A Growth feature.

     data-leed-recommendations goes on the wrapper, heading and all. That is the whole API: no helper call, no
     id, no inline script. The engine appends its cards after whatever the element already holds, so the heading
     stays above them, and when there is nothing to recommend it hides this element, which takes the heading
     with it. One element receiving both the heading and the cards means the grid is declared here and the
     heading spans it: see .recommendations in tailwind/partials/recommendations.css.

     data-preview-recommendations is a local development aid, not a production feature: it names the list page
     whose rows src/static/js/recommendations-preview.js reads to answer the engine's own request with three real
     posts, so the cards can be seen while they are being built. That script is emitted only by
     `leed site build --serve` and checks the hostname on top of that, so a deployed page never loads it and only
     the engine writes here. --}}
<section class="recommendations" data-leed-recommendations data-preview-recommendations="###LIST_URL###">
  <h2 class="recommendations__heading">Read next</h2>
</section>
